<div class="with-rail with-rail--about">
  <div>
    <h1 class="h1-display" style="margin-bottom: 24px; max-width: 16ch;">Frederic Jean</h1>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>I work at BNSF on scheduling, mostly on intermodal traffic: getting more out of each railcar, and getting the right car under the cargo at hand. It is the same problem I have always worked on &mdash; capacity, demand and timing &mdash; with heavier equipment.</p>
      <p>Before that I spent nearly nine years at AWS, on the systems that keep serverless and LLM workloads supplied with compute, storage and inference. And before that I ran my own practice out of Colorado: micro-service and service-based architecture, authentication and authorization in distributed environments, continuous delivery pipelines, test automation.</p>
      <p>I have been writing here since March 2007 &mdash; through Java, JRuby, Groovy, user-group talks, tokens, Kubernetes, a long silence, and back to gems. The archive is intact, typos and all.</p>
    </div>

    <h2 style="font-size: 24px; line-height: 1.2; margin: 44px 0 14px;">What I work on</h2>
    <ul class="prose" style="margin: 0; padding-left: 20px;">
      <li>Architecting micro-services and service based architecture</li>
      <li>Addressing authentication and authorization in distributed environments</li>
      <li>Building continuous delivery pipelines</li>
      <li>Automating tests</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 style="font-size: 24px; line-height: 1.2; margin: 44px 0 16px;">Open source</h2>
    <div class="card-grid">
      <div class="card">
        <span class="card-kicker">Ruby gem</span>
        <span class="card-title">middleman-s3_sync</span>
        <p class="card-body">Synchronizes a Middleman build to S3 and invalidates CloudFront. Currently 4.8.0.</p>
        <span class="card-meta">Maintained &middot; 2013&ndash;today</span>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <span class="card-kicker">Ruby gem</span>
        <span class="card-title">jruby-memcache-client</span>
        <p class="card-body">Memcache client for JRuby, with support for multiple connection pools.</p>
        <span class="card-meta">Archived &middot; 2009</span>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p style="margin: 20px 0 0; font-size: 16px;"><a href="https://github.com/fredjean">See everything on GitHub &rarr;</a></p>
